[h1]Phobos Auto Nav[/h1]
[h2]Flight hub display correction in 0.14.1[/h2]
Corrects missing compact labels, clipped range/speed readings and blank decrease buttons with the native font. Framework 0.21.2 restores the audited native knob/switch/slider path under BepInEx. Keeps the current five-tab hub, saved flight bindings, placement and approved artwork. Prepared offline; owner visual/gameplay confirmation remains pending.
[h2]Optional arrival cue in 0.14.0[/h2]
Requires Phobos Framework 0.21.0 or newer. Engage Approach or Rendezvous, then opt into one arrival cue through Details or F3. Stop, suspension and reload clear watches. Shared volume/mute and burst suppression; native docking sound remains unchanged. No weapon, Follow or intermediate docking-stage cues. Gameplay/listening review pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shared-completion-cues.md]Shared controls, limits and original audio provenance[/url]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.14.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - held for upstream provenance review

N1 supplies navigation/docking; N2 adds pursuit. Phobos' Asterel N3 Polaris Fire Control System independently supplies fire-control information, limited volleys and optional RCS aiming, including during manual flight without N1/N2. All combinations share one hub. Existing N2 owners now need N3 for automated firing; IDs, recipes and saved flights remain intact.

[h2]Current features[/h2]
[list]
[*]One tall graphite/slate hub exposes Navigation, Pursuit, Fire and Systems, with diagnostic-only Details. Place its new 25%-wide, 80%-high footprint through native Edit; old compact placements do not expand over other instruments. Keep native map, sensors, warnings and Comms available.
[*]Reuse native guarded switches, buttons and sliders by runtime reference. Separate navigation/offensive targets and unavailable/stale readings are explicit. No game artwork is redistributed.
[*]Header, tabs and bottom actions fit their faceplate recesses. Telemetry and settings use inset display fields; compact status labels keep full explanations in Details. Layout checks include field boundaries, not only overall panel fit.
[*]Compact page-button faces leave clear margins inside the tab row while retaining larger click targets and readable labels.
[*]Navigation offers Approach, Dock and explicit Approach & Dock: capture native clearance/assigned ports, stage 1 km beyond protected hull clearance, match motion and revalidate the RCS-only handoff. Failed handoff suspends for Resume.
[*]Systems shows essential propulsion telemetry and native torch controls. Manual actions release automation and retain native restrictions. Specialist reactor functions remain native.
[*]Predict motion over a short horizon and replan from qualified observations of both ships. Preserve RCS throttle, torch protections and braking handoff.
[*]N2: Rendezvous finishes at a chosen separation; Follow maintains a band. N3 adds a separate offensive target/group, 1–9 native volleys (default one), per-weapon readiness and guarded Engage. A volley is one successful ready-weapon batch, not one projectile or ammunition unit.
[*]N2/N3: Polaris merchant or two-electronics/30-minute construction; 0.4 kg, $5,400/$1,350 authored values, repair/Restore and retained board offcuts/residue.
[*]N3 Auto Aim separately permits RCS rotation while coasting or a heading request during N2 Follow. Braking/clearance take priority. Manual input during Auto Aim cancels aiming and firing; weapons-only authorization permits manual flight.
[*]Cease Fire and volley completion retain FCS Hold until explicit Return to Native. Native offensive queues cannot bypass the budget; defensive PDCs, unrelated groups and deliberate manual shots remain native.
[*]Choose cruise speed, arrival speed and stopping distance at each console.
[*]Use live native sensor contact, torch preference with RCS fallback, and bounded RCS throttle.
[*]Preserve flight intent and captured preferences across saves, subject to validation before resuming.
[*]Obtain the module through merchants, construction or rare native module salvage.
[/list]

[h2]Limits and save behaviour[/h2]
[list]
[*]0.12.1 is a Polaris startup correction candidate: validate the embedded hub layout with a managed reader and contain hub-construction failures so native loading can continue. Disabled native packages skip hub creation and equipment publication. The owner confirmed that reverting 0.12.0 removed the exception; gameplay confirmation of this candidate is pending.
[*]Resume, Disengage and Cease Fire remain on every page. Disengage clears thrust and allows coasting; it is not emergency braking. Approach stops short; docking requires Dock or Approach & Dock.
[*]No general obstacle avoidance, guaranteed catch or intact capture. Sensor loss suspends guidance. N1 Fly remains a one-shot approach; N2 Follow supplies continuous distance holding.
[*]Rendezvous, Follow and both combined docking phases suspend after reload. Fire permission and prediction history are never restored. Native manual/defensive settings remain in force; missile fire requires the open native display and completed lock. An invalid or over-one-second simulation interval revokes fire permission; no catch-up volleys. Reload restores group ownership as Hold, never permission or aiming. Stock 1.0.1.5 missiles lack the required automatic envelope and remain blocked; no manual-mode override or invented range is supplied. Decoys are excluded. Ordinary flight restoration follows its own validation and preference policy.
[*]Offline manoeuvring-target and fire-interlock checks pass; the tall hub, pursuit, combat coordination and moving-target docking require owner gameplay evaluation. All routine views pass offline layout checks at 300 x 480, 400 x 640 and 600 x 960; those are not native gameplay captures. Numerical results are not measured game fuel savings.
[*]Upstream-derived guidance reuse terms remain unresolved. This draft is held for provenance review before Workshop publication.
[/list]

