[h2]Research attribution[/h2]
[b]Shipbreaker industrial navigation is research only:[/b] the owner selected Auto Nav as a required dependency for the future Shipbreaker implementation, using N1 or N2 and one explicitly selected G4. The proposed service preserves one flight owner and exact native identities while aligning, holding and advancing the selected G4 against observed target geometry. Docking/capture is optional; collision-compatible reach remains unresolved. Current Auto Nav has no G4 acquisition mode, arbitrary mooring or automatic undocking.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-autopilot-research.md]G4 research and limits[/url] | [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-autopilot-handover.md]Implementation handover[/url]
[url=https://www.nasa.gov/general/nasas-hybrid-computer-enables-ravens-autonomous-rendezvous-capability/]NASA Goddard's Raven research[/url] and [url=https://www.esa.int/Science_Exploration/Human_and_Robotic_Exploration/ATV/ATV_views_Space_Station_as_never_before]ESA's LIRIS experiment by Airbus, Jena Optronik and Sodern[/url] support the sensing research direction, not claims of implemented cutting or validated gameplay.

[url=https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/1022980/view/503954886346412815]Daniel Fedor, Blue Bottle Games, July 2025 combat preview[/url] provides historical weapon-role context. Locally inspected Ostranauts 1.0.1.5 code determines current firing restrictions; this is not endorsement or validation of our FCS.
[url=https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20120014309]Zhou, NASA Langley (2012)[/url] supports relative-motion feedback; [url=https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/90483/1/orcsatpaper_final.pdf]Hartley, Trodden, Richards and Maciejowski, ESA ORCSAT (2012)[/url] motivates constrained repeated planning for a passive target; [url=https://www.esa.int/Enabling_Support/Operations/ATV_i_Jules_Verne_i]ESA ATV operations[/url] motivates separate checked approach/hold/capture phases. Our game controller, thresholds and equipment balance are authored choices; these sources neither validate nor endorse this mod or hostile capture.

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.21.2 or newer. Original Auto Navigate is not a dependency and must be disabled for Phobos Auto Nav to engage.

This is a maintained pre-publication page draft, not a download announcement. No Workshop item has been published for this draft. Use the installation guide for source/prepared-package availability and loader setup. Do not remove required providers from saves that contain their content.

